            <div class="remix-caption" id="remixCaption">An opening at the edge</div>
            <div class="id-row"><span class="id" id="remixId">cb2:a18f32…03c47e</span><span class="quiet" id="remixStatus">Changed strategy</span></div>
            <div class="allocation"><span class="asset"><i class="dot"></i>jupSOL</span><strong id="lstValue">70%</strong></div>
            <div class="allocation"><span class="asset"><i class="dot yellow"></i>USDC</span><strong id="usdcValue">30%</strong></div>
            <label class="label" for="allocation">Explore another allocation</label>
            <select class="slider" id="allocation" aria-label="Illustrative existing-vault selection or allocation draft"><option value="70">70 / 30 · another sample vault</option><option value="60">60 / 40 · same sample vault</option><option value="50">50 / 50 · unmatched draft</option></select>
            <button class="button" id="remix">Preview new expression</button>
            <p class="micro"><span id="remixExplanation">Select another existing vault; the parent stays intact.</span><br>No live purchase is available in this preview.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
    <div class="footnotes">
      <p>One share token represents managed holdings. Saved target weights remain readable; actual composition and current NAV are separate facts.</p>
      <p>Captions can be sensory, spatial, intimate, or absent. They stay small enough to let the image speak.</p>
      <p>A remix inherits a visual gesture. Select another existing vault, or keep desired weights as an explicit draft. The parent stays intact.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="footer"><span>Design artifact only. No wallet, inference, live quotes, or financial execution.<br>All shown IDs are illustrative. Color reflects composition, not risk.</span><a href="../superpowers/specs/2026-10-09-coloyond-strategy-cards-design.md">Read the specification →</a></div>
    <p class="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite" id="notice"></p>
