| **CP0 / S0** | Admission console: review versioned manifest, test-cluster mint/feed facts, solver evidence and blocked/unverified states; unmatched mint must not expose deposit. Local UI + Devnet/Testnet read-only data. |
| **CP1 / S1** | Localnet vault UI: two test-wallet deposits, receipt/share claims, failed-transfer rejection, pause and in-kind exit; Android pending action recovery without blind resend. |
| **CP2a / S2 — internal fixture QA** | Browser fixture workbench: walk eligible start → partial → final → close, exercise rejection controls and stale/paused starts; verify balances/events and synthetic/no-network labels. Presentation QA only; not a human checkpoint. |
| **CP2b / S2 — next real protocol checkpoint** | Localnet UI connected to the actual Coloyond SBF auction: use a throwaway Localnet wallet to sign start/fills/close, verify confirmed signatures and RPC account deltas, and attempt replay/wrong-feed/adverse/oversize/concurrent fills; rejected calls must leave balances unchanged. Localnet Pyth/mint fixtures are synthetic; this proves actual SBF/SPL execution, not Devnet oracle authenticity or liquidity. |
| **CP3 / S3** | Localnet condition/keeper UI plus Android card journey: advancing versus replayed/stale/expired observations; third-party transition with keepers stopped; draft→generate→save→share/import→remix and submitted/confirmed distinction. |
| **CP4 / S4 Devnet wallet and fee loop** | Runnable Android test-only route connected to the exact admitted Devnet genesis/program/vault, actual MWA wallet, and RPC-backed receipts. The Localnet SBF bootstrap/governance sequence remains a separate program test, not the wallet checkpoint. | Solana Devnet only; actual target MWA wallet and dedicated faucet-funded test signer. No mock wallet or network fallback. | After S0B asset/feed admission, S4A economics review, verified app identity and reviewed Devnet deployment are complete, verify visible Devnet genesis/program/vault/mints/revision, select an exact published test card, inspect the decoded deposit message and durable pending record, approve deposit and reconcile the confirmed transaction plus user token/share and vault custody deltas from RPC. Redeem in kind and reconcile outputs. Use the Devnet auction workbench to fill and claim an earned test bounty; reconcile fee split/reserve/liability/share backing and redeem again. Exercise wallet rejection, uncertain submission, force-stop/restart and signature recovery; require no duplicate send. If any prerequisite or the actual target wallet fails, record CP4 blocked; do not substitute Localnet fixtures, a mock or another cluster. |
| **CP5 / S5 — ETF AMM and scheduler-invocation Devnet proof** | Runnable ETF pool UI connected to the exact Solana Devnet genesis/program and actual wallet. Before seed/swap, review feed price, `publish_time`, age and confidence using the mode-specific account facts in the manifest (both modes use Pull Oracle-owned `PriceUpdateV2` and must show `Full`; fixed mode also proves its shard-zero PDA derivation and updater state). Initialize and seed the pool; make a separate trader wallet's real SPL swap; reconcile confirmed signatures, all token-account changes, shares and fee accounting from RPC. Create/fund the selected scheduler queue, register a compiled task payload, re-read its immutable task identity, then capture the external crank-turner-signed invocation transaction and resulting eligibility/maintenance state. Record queue deposit, task rent and per-crank reward separately; a refundable 1 SOL queue minimum does not prove ongoing execution funding. Show that a distinct trader-funded transaction is still required for a swap. Submit wallet-signed wrong-feed, adverse-direction and oversize transactions that reach the program; record confirmed on-chain errors and transaction fees separately, and prove token balances are unchanged. Pause risk-increasing actions and complete a wallet-signed in-kind withdrawal while risk is paused. A Devnet-created synthetic/unbacked test SPL mint is allowed only with explicit labeling; Localnet/simulator fixtures are not substitutes. If the selected L1 scheduler does not execute, CP5 remains blocked until a reviewed replacement passes the same real invocation proof.
