## Quote conservatism argument and independent review

The focused `cargo test -p coloyond-etf-math --locked` suite was rerun at `7d90186295aa99fb6ed286187b7ef5a664359acb`; all 65 unit/integration tests passed. This validates the current pure-math crate test corpus, not the Android changes, integrated ETF program, token CPI, or a Devnet transaction.

After adding the 29,106-row post-fee drift matrix, `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `cargo test -p coloyond-etf-math --locked` and `git diff --check` passed; the focused crate ran 67 unit/integration tests. An initial concurrent run overlapped CSV regeneration and observed a truncated include file; after generation completed, the sequential rerun passed. A follow-up NAV-accounting assertion records the 28,999 modeled NAV-loss cases without treating composition improvement as economic safety. The initial Q96 audit added 59,511 high-precision reference rows (12 log, 99 exponential and 59,400 power cases) over 4,950 valid two/three-asset weight pairs and twelve boundary-oriented base points; two generator runs produced SHA-256 `d2dd71d2937e1a23afb2e08844e608cdfd8f9c7aef5fe0f99abc20d907b71626`. Python `Decimal` at 130 digits is a high-precision reference, not rigorous interval arithmetic; this corpus corroborates the analytical proof but is finite base/exponent sampling. After those additions, `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `cargo test -p coloyond-etf-math --locked` passed with 68 unit/integration tests. These runs validate only the pure-math candidate and checked-in vectors, not Android compilation, the integrated ETF program, token CPI, or a Devnet transaction.

For a supported exact-in swap, the gross input is at most 30% of the input reserve and the fee-adjusted input is no larger than gross. Therefore the exact reserve ratio `B_in / (B_in + net_in)` is at least `10/13`. The weight ratio is at most 99 because weights sum to 10,000 bps and every weight is at least 100 bps. Thus `-ln(base) × weight_in / weight_out < -ln(10/13) × 99 < 26`, the documented exponential domain.

The implementation rounds the reserve ratio up, the lower bound for `-ln(base)` down, and the exponent down. Its atanh-series terms round down and the omitted terms are nonnegative. For `exp(-z)`, it reduces `z` by flooring division by 256, evaluates the alternating Taylor series through even degree 12 on an argument below 0.102, and rounds positive terms and each of eight squarings up. These directions produce an upper bound for the curve power; subtracting from one and multiplying the output reserve with floor rounding produces an output no larger than the exact weighted-curve result. Because gross input is retained while only fee-adjusted input is priced, ideal invariant nondecrease follows for exact custody deltas. This is a mathematical argument for the bounded quote construction, not a substitute for broader implementation/property evidence or on-chain custody tests.

An independent read-only code review found no arithmetic unsoundness in the inspected quote/deviation paths and agreed the conservative-rounding argument is plausible over this domain. Since that review, generated coverage has been expanded: exact deviation vectors now cover two and three assets; 29,106 generated three-asset swaps cover all 100-bps target-weight partitions and all ordered asset pairs, with varied marks, decimals, fees and sizes, checking exact curve bounds and same-snapshot USD drift improvement; 240 two-asset cases check the exact integer invariant at the maximum 99:1 weight ratio; 2,976 three-asset quotes cover the minimum-weight boundary; and 4,096 full-width two-asset samples compare against an exact integer custody-invariant bound. The new fixed-array share module implements the frozen initial NAV issuance, proportional deposit/refund, and in-kind redemption formulas; six integration tests cover 256 generated two/three-asset transitions and per-asset backing monotonicity under integer rounding. This is pure-math accounting evidence only, not token CPI/custody evidence. The expanded 79,466-row high-precision Q96 kernel corpus checks sampled log lower, exponential upper and weighted-power upper bounds against the analytical error ledger, including every exponential range-reduction transition; independent review found no defect in its vectors or one-sided assertions. Its Decimal references and sampled base/exponent values do not establish a rigorous full-domain interval certificate. Remaining gaps include full-domain fixed-point error coverage, integrated target-runtime compute, actual SBF custody/share reconciliation, and real transaction evidence. The Python standard-library generators make the selected math vectors reproducible; the focused share transition table is generated deterministically in Rust and independently checked against the frozen integer formulas.

