**Interfaces:** `RpcConfig(endpoint: String)` with session/optional secure handling and redacted diagnostics; an injected `RpcClient` for account/status/history/transaction/simulation reads, built on the existing `core/rpc` transport. `VaultRef(network, protocol, programId, vaultAddress, shareMint)`; `VaultObservation(ref, targetWeights, actualWeights, configDigest, configProjection, programDeploySlot, nav, authorities, fees, rebalanceRules, observedAtMs, slot, keeperEvidence)`. `nav` is a sealed available/unavailable type with decimal USD-per-share and source when available. `ProtocolAdapter.readVault(ref: VaultRef): VaultObservation` and `readKeeperEvidence(ref: VaultRef): KeeperEvidence` are `suspend` functions that use the injected `RpcClient`. `KeeperEvidence` includes last observed settled activity signature/time or an unavailable reason. A separately versioned release manifest carries the exact account layout and `configProjectionVersion`, verified deployment slot, Metis decoder/program allowlist, supported vault refs, keeper thresholds, and smoke-tested recovery capability. Published versions are frozen; observations and reverse quotes are runtime records outside the manifest and strategy hash. The catalog consists of its supported refs loaded through `readVault`, not runtime unrestricted scans. These are client-owned interfaces, not SDK method names.

