# Coloyond on-chain portfolio rebalancing: agent sprint checklist

**Status:** execution checklist, not evidence that a vault or funded flow exists.  
**Companion architecture:** [on-chain portfolio rebalancing plan](onchain-portfolio-rebalancing-plan.md).  
**Schedule assumption:** Sprint 0 is a proof block; Sprints 1–4 complete the current auction path and card product; Sprint 5 adds a separately versioned ETF AMM; Sprints 6–7 cover security and Devnet readiness; Sprints 8–10 are later expansions. The former 13-week estimate is withdrawn and must be re-baselined for both protocol paths, staffing, evidence and audit gates.

**Active session override (11 October 2026):** The user authorized implementation to continue past human checkpoint pauses until they ask to stop. This changes scheduling only: no checkpoint or funded/release gate is accepted or waived. CP2a is synthetic browser QA only; CP2b remains the next real protocol checkpoint and requires a browser Localnet wallet walkthrough of actual SBF/SPL auction transactions, confirmed RPC signatures and token-account deltas. The bootstrap and S4C Localnet harnesses prove real program execution against synthetic mint/oracle fixtures, not authenticated Pyth or Devnet admission. S0B remains held and S4A remains `NO_GO`. S4E2 durable signing/reconciliation was implemented and pushed as `b663bab`. S4E3 now has a read-only Devnet portfolio route for vault and connected-wallet SPL balances, oracle observations, risk blockers and pending-action reconciliation; it exposes no transaction action and excludes demo-wallet addresses from on-chain lookups. Android Gradle validation is unavailable in the active shell: a JDK 17 installation exists outside the active Java configuration, the Gradle wrapper distribution is not cached, network access is unavailable, and no Android SDK/platform is configured. The actual target-wallet/app-identity recovery proof remains open. CP4 is a Devnet wallet checkpoint because the app's MWA adapter binds to Devnet and the standard MWA chain identifiers do not include Localnet; S0B, S4A, deployment and app-identity gates currently block it. The user has temporarily waived pauses, not evidence gates or funded-action restrictions.

**Colleague branch integration:** `f2a1a5ee522881426298b01f3ca49fc5aeeba73c` was superseded on the remote by `ee443d231050b305f9b00a7d97b7034ade607c21`, which is the fetched integration target. Preserve the Symmetry code as a separate Devnet-only comparison; it is not the custody core and cannot satisfy CP2b or Coloyond S2C/S2E. The comparison UI currently reads only and exposes no signing action. The colleague's separate no-backend ETF proposal is preserved in [the blueprint](blueprints/no-backend-auto-rebalancing-multi-token-etf-solana-devnet.md) and is elevated into Sprint 5 as an isolated second protocol pillar. Its original claims remain proposal text; the active decisions and evidence gates in this checklist govern implementation.

## 1. Mission, source of truth, and scope

Deliver the old spec's complete **choose allocation → generate expression → save → share/import → remix** Android experience; preserve the current v0.3.0 curated two-asset WSOL/USDC vault and permissionless Dutch-auction path; and add the colleague's multi-token weighted-mean ETF AMM as a separate v1 foundation protocol in Sprint 5. Each version owns its account layouts, IDL, manifests, strategy identity, clients, invariant tests and security evidence. No work unit may quietly merge their settlement logic or mutate v0.3.0. The creative experience remains useful when finance is unavailable. Keepers/crank-turners provide replaceable liveness only, with no custody or policy authority. Android is the explicit wallet-signing client; the browser may show independently sourced, labeled facts. A keeper, SDK, RPC service, API or UI cannot make an invalid transition valid: each program enforces its own financial conditions.

**Modularity is a sprint-wide contract:** every work unit owns a bounded package/write set, consumes a versioned interface, and produces its own evidence. Parallel work starts only after its shared interface is frozen; integration belongs to a named owner and may not reach into another package's internals. Each protocol version remains independently buildable, testable, deployable and replaceable at its SDK/oracle/scheduler boundaries.

**Precedence for this mission:** the reviewed [card specification](../superpowers/specs/2026-10-09-coloyond-strategy-cards-design.md) and its [implementation plan](../superpowers/plans/2026-10-09-coloyond-managed-strategies.md) govern card identity, expression, client privacy, truthful observations, import/share/remix and mobile recovery. The user's newer fully on-chain direction replaces only their hackathon restriction on building a vault/keeper and their Symmetry/Jupiter financial execution path. [The new on-chain plan](onchain-portfolio-rebalancing-plan.md) governs that replacement protocol after Sprint 0 publishes its versioned product/risk amendment. Do not erase the old spec or reinterpret its `cb2:` records. The cross-chain swap draft is a separate vision and does not override either reviewed contract.

