## 8. Sprint 5 — isolated multi-token ETF AMM foundation

This is a new first-class protocol pillar, not a refactor of the current auction vault. Preserve the original [colleague blueprint](blueprints/no-backend-auto-rebalancing-multi-token-etf-solana-devnet.md) as the proposal record; implement only the evidence-backed contract in the companion plan and the Sprint 5A freeze. The adopted core is a multi-token weighted-mean AMM, oracle-anchored swaps, a fee/share ledger, and replaceable scheduled maintenance. One deliberate architecture change is required: a scheduler can call `poke` and record eligibility, but it cannot supply the opposite SPL asset or cause a swap without a counterparty. Therefore the scheduled `rebalance()`-as-trade proposal is replaced with scheduler-triggered eligibility plus separate permissionless, trader-funded swaps. No project-operated backend or personal bot is required for that path, but third-party crank, RPC, oracle-publisher and trader availability remain off-chain dependencies. Do not promise zero off-chain infrastructure, autonomous trading without a counterparty, “up-only” returns or protection implied by a fee table. The target is a real Devnet pool with explicit, accurately labeled test assets and wallet-signed transactions; Localnet and simulator data are not accepted as CP5 substitutes.

**S5A authority amendment selected:** permissionless deterministic pool creation uses the initializer only as rent payer; distinct nonzero initial governance/guardian keys are included in the canonical config hash and pool PDA. Funding clients verify the complete reviewed hash/tuple first. Exact-approved-pool front-run is safe: clients verify the immutable readback and continue; a substituted tuple derives a different pool. Literal authority keys remain deployment blockers. On 11 October 2026, the configured public RPC and independent OnFinality RPC returned `EtWTRAB...` at adjacent slots, matching the Solana SDK constant. The Solana docs example prints `GH7ome...`; record the discrepancy and pin the live endpoint identity. Current-cluster account reads and SDK parser decoding pass, but the latest finalized Devnet basket remains freshness-blocked: slot `509744939` found all three feeds 166 seconds old against the diagnostic 60-second limit. Three Mainnet samples passed that limit at 10, 42 and 33 seconds, but do not establish ongoing freshness. Pyth's 55-second push heartbeat is not a delivery SLA; preserve fail-closed staleness behavior and resolve updater path before S5E.

**S5 gate sequence:** S5B may complete independent parameterized math review, S5C may prove oracle parser/account behavior, and S5D2 may gather candidate economic evidence without selecting production settings. The user has re-prioritized Sprint 5 and authorized fail-closed S5E code/host/Localnet work and independent S5F/S5G read-only client/UI work against explicit draft inputs. This supersedes the earlier rule that no S5E code could start before policy freeze; it does not accept any gate or authorize deployment, pool initialization, seed, swap, or funded Devnet use. S5A still owns final contract/policy acceptance, incorporating math, oracle/risk, and fee/economics findings. Keep stale/out-of-policy feeds and all unapproved risk-increasing actions fail-closed.
**Current S5 vertical-slice status (11 October 2026):** The draft profile recommendation is WSOL/Test USD at 50/50, with the second mint explicitly synthetic, unbacked, and not redeemable as USDC; it is not admitted. S5C finalized captures prove exact account parser/feed identity and Full verification but the latest Devnet feeds are stale under the 60-second diagnostic. The S5E audit found the identity/math minimum-weight mismatch and the 1e18/1e12 scale mismatch; the bounded resolution is recorded in the [S5 profile evidence](../rebalancing/evidence/s5-devnet-test-profile.md). S5A weight-floor fix and S5F are integrated at `b11419e` with 31 passing package tests and a passing typecheck. A finalized live RPC read at slot `509792525` verified the pinned genesis and exact candidate account identities; fixed feeds were Full but 228 seconds old under an unconfigured freshness policy. No ETF program, pool, deployment ID, connected wallet, or Devnet ETF transaction exists yet. The immediate target is a real frontend RPC/wallet read followed by safe transaction readiness; no submitted or timed-out signature will be reported successful without confirmed RPC reconciliation. The S5F receipt helper now enforces this for its tested signature, fee, and tracked-token metadata path; pool/share/fee readback and real wallet transactions remain unproven.

The authority-bound identity amendment is now present in the Rust/Python encoders and synthetic fixture: both keys are validated, serialized, hashed, and included in pool seeds. The previous provisional fixture hash `0852ddf87df71fb53c07f235c4afbf11c4593ced710807ac208427b0c10ecf72` is superseded and is not a canonical `etf1:` identity. Before S5E, freeze the on-chain acceptance criteria and cross-language vectors for canonical hash/role binding, delayed handoff, exact-init retry, and third-party PDA pre-funding. S5E must prove these behaviors against the actual program with account readbacks and atomic-failure assertions; they cannot be demonstrated before the program exists. Literal deployment keys remain a deployment blocker.

